# Runtime state and logs live on the host, never in git (the predecessor repo
# died from committed secrets/state). Subtrees that also carry runtime state keep
# their own .gitignore (daemon/, instance/decisions/); this root list covers the
# orchestrator runtime dir the ops journal and lane state live in, plus the
# repo-root runtime dir the tmux launcher puts the singleton lock and state.db in
# (unignored it left the tree permanently dirty, so every session load reported
# `startup: degraded` and the real signal was lost).
orchestrator/runtime/
/runtime/
# Per-host launcher configuration (ports, chat binding, provider/model choice for
# THIS box). It is sourced by orchestrator/*.sh and overrides the environment, so
# it is host state by definition and a natural place for someone to paste a chat
# id or token. The tracked contract is runtime.env.example; defaults that must
# survive a fresh clone belong in launch.sh, not here.
orchestrator/runtime.env
# Backups of the above. Recovery on 2026-08-04 left runtime.env.bak-oldorch-20260804
# beside it; the exact-path rule did not cover it, so `git add -A` would have staged a
# copy of the one file this list exists to keep out. Same content, same risk, so the
# same rule must cover every backup of it.
orchestrator/runtime.env.*
# ...except the tracked contract. Broad rule plus this negation, rather than a narrow
# bak-only glob, so a backup named .old/.save/.2 is covered too.
!orchestrator/runtime.env.example

# Harness-created git worktrees for isolated agent lanes. They hold checkouts of
# this same repo, so leaving them untracked made `git status` dirty for the whole
# session and buried the real signal — the same failure mode as the repo-root
# runtime dir above.
.claude/worktrees/

node_modules/
*.log

# Ephemeral stand workspaces created by morning.sh / stand scenarios
stand/workspaces/
